===Etymology 1===
Often thought to be modified from ''bl'' for ''barrel'' ''(b[[⸺]]l)'', reflecting a way of abbreviating that was used especially in previous centuries (compare {{m|en|do#Etymology 3|do}} for {{m|en|ditto}}), wherein a doubled letter indicated plural count, as also with {{m|en|p.}}=page but {{m|en|pp.}}=pages and {{m|en|l.}}=line but {{m|en|ll.}}=lines; this method was used not only in English but also in scholarly New Latin and other modern languages heavily affected thereby, such as with Spanish {{m|es|EE. UU.}} According to this idea, addition of the suffix {{m|en|-s}}, as sometimes seen (e.g., ''5 bbls'' or ''5 bbls.''), would seem to have come from writers who left the unit abbreviation itself unanalyzed (unparsed), thus adding a {{l|en|venial#Adjective|venially}} redundant marker of plural, somewhat like with ''MPGs'' for ''miles per gallon''.

